#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"platform-sep26\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "September 2026 {#september-2026}"
msgstr "Setyembre 2026 {#september-2026}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The first Nighthawk r2 QPU is now available** &mdash; Premium, Flex, and Pay-As-You-Go Plans now have access to `ibm_phoenix`, the first IBM Quantum Nighthawk r2 QPU and our fastest processor yet. `ibm_phoenix` is a high-connectivity, square-lattice 120-programmable-qubit device that delivers up to 25× higher throughput than Heron while matching its fidelity. \n"
msgstr "**Available na ngayon ang unang Nighthawk r2 QPU** &mdash; Ang mga Premium, Flex, at Pay-As-You-Go Plans ay may access na ngayon sa `ibm_phoenix`, ang unang IBM Quantum Nighthawk r2 QPU at ang pinakamabilis naming processor sa ngayon. Ang `ibm_phoenix` ay isang high-connectivity, square-lattice na 120-programmable-qubit device na naghahatid ng hanggang 25× na mas mataas na throughput kaysa sa Heron habang tinutugma ang fidelity nito. \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The gains come from a newly introduced independent high-speed reset that returns every programmable qubit to the ground state faster and more completely. As a result, the default repetition delay is 1 µs (previously 250 µs), which pushes throughput above 100,000 Max Circuits Per Second (MCPS). For more about how IBM tracks quantum hardware performance across metrics of scale, quality, and speed, see [this blog](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/hardware-metrics-2026).\n"
msgstr "  Ang mga pakinabang ay nagmumula sa bagong ipinakilalang independent high-speed reset na nagbabalik sa bawat programmable qubit sa ground state nang mas mabilis at mas kumpleto. Bilang resulta, 1 µs na ang default repetition delay (mula sa dating 250 µs), na nagtutulak sa throughput nang higit sa 100,000 Max Circuits Per Second (MCPS). Para sa karagdagang impormasyon kung paano tinatrack ng IBM ang performance ng quantum hardware sa mga metrics ng scale, quality, at speed, tingnan ang [blog na ito](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/hardware-metrics-2026).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The increased speed and connectivity make it possible to do more usable work from the same capacity, with the largest, most demanding workloads benefitting the most. Larger experiments, broader parameter sweeps, and methods that were once too costly at scale are now practical to run routinely.\n"
msgstr "  Ang pinataas na bilis at connectivity ay nagpapahintulot na gawin ang mas maraming magagamit na gawain mula sa parehong kapasidad, kung saan ang pinakamalaki at pinakamahihirap na workload ang pinakamakikinabang. Ang mas malalaking eksperimento, mas malawak na parameter sweep, at mga paraan na dati ay masyadong magastos sa malaking sukat ay maisasagawa na ngayon nang regular.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  `ibm_phoenix` is also built for the next era of quantum error correction research. Alongside high-speed reset, it supports mid-circuit reset and dynamic circuits for real-time control over error correction.\n"
msgstr "  Ang `ibm_phoenix` ay binuo rin para sa susunod na yugto ng pananaliksik sa quantum error correction. Kasama ng high-speed reset, sinusuportahan nito ang mid-circuit reset at dynamic circuits para sa real-time control sa error correction.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"platform-aug26\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "August 2026 {#august-2026}"
msgstr "Agosto 2026 {#august-2026}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Updates to IBM Quantum Platform** &mdash; A recent update to IBM Quantum Platform makes it easier to understand your job results, unlocks powerful new circuit design capabilities in Composer, and keeps you informed about your usage limits — so you can focus more on your quantum work.\n"
msgstr "**Mga update sa IBM Quantum Platform** &mdash; Ang kamakailang update sa IBM Quantum Platform ay nagpapadali sa pag-unawa sa mga resulta ng iyong job, nag-a-unlock ng makapangyarihang bagong kakayahan sa disenyo ng circuit sa Composer, at pinapanatili kang updated tungkol sa iyong usage limits — upang mas makatuon ka sa iyong quantum work.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Job results & workloads  \n"
msgstr "Mga resulta ng job at workload  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Bit-by-bit outcomes view** — a new way to view Sampler measurement results, breaking down outcomes bit by bit instead of by full state. Useful as an alternative to the Measurement outcomes view when results contain many distinct states.  \n"
msgstr "**Bit-by-bit outcomes view** — isang bagong paraan para tingnan ang mga resulta ng pagsukat ng Sampler, hinahati ang mga outcome bit por bit sa halip na buong estado. Kapaki-pakinabang bilang alternatibo sa Measurement outcomes view kapag ang mga resulta ay naglalaman ng maraming magkakaibang estado.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Circuit timing chart** — shows a scheduled timeline of a circuit's operations (gates, channels, durations). Available for Sampler and Executor jobs. Requires [enabling timing data retrieval](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing#enable-timing-data-retrieval).  \n"
msgstr "**Circuit timing chart** — nagpapakita ng naka-iskedyul na timeline ng mga operasyon ng circuit (gates, channels, durations). Available para sa Sampler at Executor jobs. Kailangan ang [pag-enable ng timing data retrieval](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/qiskit-runtime-circuit-timing#enable-timing-data-retrieval).  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Chunk/span execution diagnostics panel** — a new panel on job details showing chunk- and span-level execution diagnostics. See [Sampler input/output](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/sampler-input-output) for what this data means and how to enable it when submitting jobs.  \n"
msgstr "**Chunk/span execution diagnostics panel** — isang bagong panel sa job details na nagpapakita ng chunk- at span-level execution diagnostics. Tingnan ang [Sampler input/output](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/sampler-input-output) para malaman kung ano ang ibig sabihin ng datos na ito at kung paano ito i-enable kapag nagsu-submit ng mga job.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Device calibration data at a glance** — job details now show the device calibration data from the time of submission or execution via a \"View calibration history\" link.  \n"
msgstr "**Device calibration data at a glance** — ipinapakita na ngayon ng job details ang device calibration data mula sa oras ng pagsumite o pagpapatupad sa pamamagitan ng isang \"View calibration history\" link.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Executor results visualization** — job details pages now render results for Executor jobs. See the [Directed execution model (beta)](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/directed-execution-model) guide for more on Executor.  \n"
msgstr "**Executor results visualization** — nag-render na ngayon ang mga pahina ng job details ng mga resulta para sa Executor jobs. Tingnan ang [Directed execution model (beta)](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/guides/directed-execution-model) guide para sa karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa Executor.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dynamic circuits now render on job details** — with OpenQASM 3.0 support in Composer (see more below), circuits that previously failed to render (for example, those using dynamic circuits) now display correctly on the job details page.  \n"
msgstr "**Dynamic circuits now render on job details** — sa OpenQASM 3.0 support sa Composer (tingnan pa sa ibaba), ang mga circuit na dati ay nabigo sa pag-render (halimbawa, ang mga gumagamit ng dynamic circuits) ay tama na ngayong nagpapakita sa job details page.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Histogram improvements** — faster loading, smoother zoom in/out, and a new selection tool for narrowing in on specific result ranges.  \n"
msgstr "**Histogram improvements** — mas mabilis na pag-load, mas maayos na zoom in/out, at bagong selection tool para sa pagpokus sa mga tiyak na saklaw ng resulta.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**`qiskit-ibm-runtime` code snippets in job results** — copy-ready code to retrieve a job by ID; for Executor jobs, an additional snippet lets you replicate the job.  \n"
msgstr "**`qiskit-ibm-runtime` code snippets in job results** — handa nang gamitin na code para kunin ang isang job gamit ang ID; para sa Executor jobs, may karagdagang snippet na nagbibigay-daan sa iyong kopyahin ang job.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Custom date range filter** added to the workloads table.  \n"
msgstr "**Custom date range filter** idinagdag sa workloads table.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Clickable instance names and tags** in workload detail pages, linking to the related resource.  \n"
msgstr "**Clickable instance names and tags** sa workload detail pages, na nag-uugnay sa kaugnay na resource.  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Navigate to your results on the [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page to see these improvements.  \n"
msgstr "    Pumunta sa iyong mga resulta sa [Workloads](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/workloads) page para makita ang mga pagpapabuti na ito.  \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composer: OpenQASM v3.0 support  \n"
msgstr "Composer: OpenQASM v3.0 support  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Composer now supports OpenQASM v3.0, adding:  \n"
msgstr "    Sinusuportahan na ngayon ng Composer ang OpenQASM v3.0, na nagdaragdag ng:  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Gate modifiers** — ctrl, inv, pow, etc.  \n"
msgstr "**Gate modifiers** — ctrl, inv, pow, atbp.  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Loops** — for and while  \n"
msgstr "**Loops** — for at while  \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Conditional logic** — if/else  \n"
msgstr "**Conditional logic** — if/else  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Box annotations** — group and label sections of a circuit  \n"
msgstr "**Box annotations** — pagsasama-sama at paglalagay ng label sa mga seksyon ng circuit  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Also included: smoother rendering for large circuits, and a fix for PNG exports failing on large circuits.  \n"
msgstr "    Kasama rin dito: mas maayos na rendering para sa malalaking circuit, at ayos para sa pagkabigo ng PNG exports sa malalaking circuit.  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Visit the [Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) to explore this new update.\n"
msgstr "  Bisitahin ang [Composer](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/composer) para tuklasin ang bagong update na ito.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Instance usage limits  \n"
msgstr "Instance usage limits  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Premium and Open Plan instances that hit their usage limit now display the exact date access resumes, based on the rolling usage window.  \n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita na ngayon ng Premium at Open Plan instances na umabot sa kanilang usage limit ang eksaktong petsa kung kailan magpapatuloy ang access, batay sa rolling usage window.  \n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See more on your [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.  \n"
msgstr "  Tingnan pa sa iyong [Instances](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/instances) page.  \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "July 2026 {#july-2026}"
msgstr "July 2026 {#july-2026}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"qr-rename\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit Runtime rename {#qiskit-runtime-rename}"
msgstr "Qiskit Runtime rename {#qiskit-runtime-rename}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Qiskit Runtime service is now IBM Quantum Compute Service** &mdash; This is a naming change only and does not require any code changes or updates to existing applications. You might notice the new name throughout the user interface and documentation.\n"
msgstr "**Qiskit Runtime service is now IBM Quantum Compute Service** &mdash; Isa lamang itong pagbabago sa pangalan at hindi nangangailangan ng anumang pagbabago sa code o mga update sa mga umiiral nang application. Maaaring mapansin mo ang bagong pangalan sa buong user interface at dokumentasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Historically, the term _Qiskit Runtime_ was used to refer to three related but distinct concepts.\n"
msgstr "    Sa nakaraan, ang terminong _Qiskit Runtime_ ay ginamit upang tukuyin ang tatlong magkaugnay ngunit magkaibang konsepto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Any hardware provider that wants Qiskit users to run workloads on its quantum computers must provide two provider-specific components:\n"
msgstr "    Anumang hardware provider na gustong magpatakbo ang mga user ng Qiskit ng mga workload sa kanilang mga quantum computer ay dapat magbigay ng dalawang bahaging tiyak sa provider:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Qiskit SDK extension, which enables users to submit jobs to the provider. In IBM's case, this is the open-source `qiskit-ibm-runtime` library. Rather than communicating directly with the quantum computer, it submits jobs to a cloud API.\n"
msgstr "Isang Qiskit SDK extension, na nagbibigay-daan sa mga user na magsumite ng mga job sa provider. Sa kaso ng IBM, ito ang open-source na `qiskit-ibm-runtime` library. Sa halip na direktang makipag-ugnayan sa quantum computer, nagsusumite ito ng mga job sa isang cloud API.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A runtime execution environment, which runs on the quantum computer itself. This component understands Qiskit primitives, translates them into hardware-specific operations, and executes them on the quantum hardware. In IBM's case, this is IBM Qiskit Runtime.\n"
msgstr "Isang runtime execution environment, na tumatakbo mismo sa quantum computer. Nauunawaan ng bahaging ito ang mga primitive ng Qiskit, isinasalin ang mga ito sa mga operasyong tiyak sa hardware, at isinasagawa ang mga ito sa quantum hardware. Sa kaso ng IBM, ito ang IBM Qiskit Runtime.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Between these two components sits a third element: the managed cloud service that receives jobs from the `qiskit-ibm-runtime` SDK and orchestrates their execution. This service is responsible for capabilities such as authentication, scheduling, queue management, workload routing, usage tracking, limits, and analytics. It does not process Qiskit primitives itself; instead, it dispatches workloads to the appropriate quantum computer, where the runtime execution environment performs the actual execution.\n"
msgstr "    Sa pagitan ng dalawang bahaging ito ay may ikatlong elemento: ang managed cloud service na tumatanggap ng mga job mula sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime` SDK at nag-oorkestra ng kanilang pagpapatupad. Ang serbisyong ito ang responsable para sa mga kakayahan tulad ng authentication, scheduling, queue management, workload routing, usage tracking, limits, at analytics. Hindi nito pinoproseso mismo ang mga primitive ng Qiskit; sa halip, ipinapadala nito ang mga workload sa naaangkop na quantum computer, kung saan isinasagawa ng runtime execution environment ang aktwal na pagpapatupad.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Historically, this cloud service was also called Qiskit Runtime Service, even though it is conceptually different from the runtime itself. This dual use of the term Qiskit Runtime &mdash; to describe both the execution environment and the managed cloud service &mdash; blurred the architecture and made it difficult to distinguish the open-source components from the managed cloud offering.\n"
msgstr "    Sa nakaraan, ang cloud service na ito ay tinatawag ding Qiskit Runtime Service, kahit na konseptwal itong naiiba sa runtime mismo. Ang dobleng paggamit na ito ng terminong Qiskit Runtime &mdash; upang ilarawan pareho ang execution environment at ang managed cloud service &mdash; ay nagpalabo sa arkitektura at nagpahirap na makilala ang mga open-source na bahagi mula sa managed cloud offering.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Renaming Qiskit Runtime Service to IBM Quantum Compute Service resolves this ambiguity. The resulting architecture becomes much clearer:\n"
msgstr "    Ang pagpapalit ng pangalan ng Qiskit Runtime Service sa IBM Quantum Compute Service ay lumulutas sa kalabuang ito. Ang naging arkitektura ay naging mas malinaw:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-ibm-runtime`: the open-source Qiskit extension that submits workloads.\n"
msgstr "`qiskit-ibm-runtime`: ang open-source na Qiskit extension na nagsusumite ng mga workload.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Compute Service: the managed cloud service that authenticates, schedules, manages, and routes workloads.\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Compute Service: ang managed cloud service na nag-a-authenticate, nag-iiskedyul, namamahala, at nagruruta ng mga workload.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Qiskit Runtime (or IBM Qiskit Runtime Execution Environment): the execution environment running on the quantum computer that processes and executes Qiskit primitives.\n"
msgstr "IBM Qiskit Runtime (o IBM Qiskit Runtime Execution Environment): ang execution environment na tumatakbo sa quantum computer na nagpoproseso at nagsasagawa ng mga primitive ng Qiskit.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "May 2026 {#may-2026}"
msgstr "May 2026 {#may-2026}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"store-instruction\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store instruction {#store-instruction}"
msgstr "Store instruction {#store-instruction}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Support for the [Store](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#store) instruction on IBM&reg; QPUs** - Now you can simplify complex classical computations in your quantum circuits with the Store instruction.\n"
msgstr "**Support for the [Store](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/circuit#store) instruction on IBM&reg; QPUs** - Ngayon ay maaari mo nang gawing mas simple ang mga kumplikadong klasikal na kalkulasyon sa iyong mga quantum circuit gamit ang Store instruction.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute a classical expression mid-circuit and save the result to a variable or register, which can then immediately control subsequent quantum gates.  Instead of deeply nested inline expressions, you can break computations into named intermediate steps, so that complex classical feedback logic is easier to read and maintain. **Common use cases** include the following:\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang isang klasikal na expression sa gitna ng circuit at i-save ang resulta sa isang variable o register, na maaari nang direktang kumontrol sa mga susunod na quantum gate. Sa halip na malalim na nested inline expression, maaari mong hatiin ang mga kalkulasyon sa mga pinangalanang intermediate step, para mas madaling basahin at panatilihin ang kumplikadong klasikal na feedback logic. Kasama sa **karaniwang mga use case** ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic circuits with mid-circuit measurements and classical feedback  \n"
msgstr "Dynamic circuits na may mid-circuit measurements at klasikal na feedback  \n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '      * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Long-range entanglement preparation  \n"
msgstr "Long-range entanglement preparation  \n"

#. type: Bullet: '      * '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complex conditional logic based on measurement outcomes\n"
msgstr "Kumplikadong conditional logic batay sa mga resulta ng measurement\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    To use the store instruction, first ensure you're running the latest version of `qiskit-ibm-runtime` (`pip install --upgrade qiskit-ibm-runtime`), then see the [documentation](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow#store) for more information and an example.\n"
msgstr "    Upang gamitin ang store instruction, siguraduhin munang gumagamit ka ng pinakabagong bersyon ng `qiskit-ibm-runtime` (`pip install --upgrade qiskit-ibm-runtime`), pagkatapos ay tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](/guides/classical-feedforward-and-control-flow#store) para sa karagdagang impormasyon at halimbawa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "    *Note that before submitting jobs, you should verify compatibility with each primitive's options in the documentation*: [Sampler options](/guides/sampler-options) | [Estimator options](/guides/estimator-options) | [Executor options](/guides/executor-options)\n"
msgstr "    *Tandaan na bago magsumite ng mga job, dapat mong i-verify ang compatibility sa mga option ng bawat primitive sa dokumentasyon*: [Sampler options](/guides/sampler-options) | [Estimator options](/guides/estimator-options) | [Executor options](/guides/executor-options)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "April 2026 {#april-2026}"
msgstr "April 2026 {#april-2026}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"classroom-accounts\"></span>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Classroom accounts {#classroom-accounts}"
msgstr "Classroom accounts {#classroom-accounts}"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**New Classroom Accounts**: Professors can now request a [Classroom Account](/guides/classroom-accounts) to manage and facilitate access for their students. With Classroom Accounts, students can use Open Plan resources without needing to provide personal credit card information.\n"
msgstr "**New Classroom Accounts**: Maaari na ngayong humiling ang mga propesor ng [Classroom Account](/guides/classroom-accounts) upang pamahalaan at pasimplehin ang access para sa kanilang mga estudyante. Sa Classroom Accounts, magagamit ng mga estudyante ang mga resource ng Open Plan nang hindi kailangang magbigay ng personal na impormasyon sa credit card.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**New export options now available in IBM Quantum**: Introducing new export capabilities that make it easier for account administrators to analyze, share, and work with their data.\n"
msgstr "**New export options now available in IBM Quantum**: Ipinapakilala ang bagong mga kakayahan sa pag-export na ginagawang mas madali para sa mga account administrator na suriin, ibahagi, at gamitin ang kanilang datos.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "New in the [Analytics](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics) page:\n"
msgstr "Bago sa [Analytics](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/analytics) page:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can now export charts in SVG or PNG format.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo nang i-export ang mga chart sa SVG o PNG format.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can export all analytics data, including the data behind the charts, as CSV.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mong i-export ang lahat ng analytics data, kasama ang datos sa likod ng mga chart, bilang CSV.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "      Find the export menu at the top-right corner of each card on the page.\n"
msgstr "      Hanapin ang export menu sa kanang itaas na sulok ng bawat card sa page.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "New in the [Access management](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/users) page:\n"
msgstr "Bago sa [Access management](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/users) page:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Export both the Users table and the Access Groups table in CSV format.\n"
msgstr "I-export ang parehong Users table at Access Groups table sa CSV format.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "      Find the export menu at the top-right corner of the table.\n"
msgstr "      Hanapin ang export menu sa kanang itaas na sulok ng table.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**New resources and hardware for Open Plan users**: The [IBM Quantum Open Plan](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products) now features new learning resources, new hardware, and a special one-time promotion for eligible users.\n"
msgstr "**New resources and hardware for Open Plan users**: Ang [IBM Quantum Open Plan](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/products) ay mayroon na ngayong bagong mga learning resource, bagong hardware, at isang espesyal na one-time promotion para sa mga kwalipikadong user.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "A new course, [Designing and leading quantum projects](/learning/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-projects), is now available. This course covers key topics for users looking to develop or secure funding for a quantum project, including early-stage planning, team roles and responsibilities, identifying meaningful use cases, defining measures of success, and a guide to grant writing best practices.\n"
msgstr "Isang bagong kurso, [Designing and leading quantum projects](/learning/courses/designing-and-leading-quantum-projects), ay available na ngayon. Sinasaklaw ng kursong ito ang mga pangunahing paksa para sa mga user na gustong bumuo o makakuha ng pondo para sa isang quantum project, kabilang ang maagang pagpaplano, mga tungkulin at responsibilidad ng team, pagtukoy ng makabuluhang use case, pagtukoy ng mga sukatan ng tagumpay, at gabay sa mga pinakamahusay na kasanayan sa pagsulat ng grant.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Heron r2 [`ibm_kingston`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_kingston)&mdash;one of our highest-performing quantum computers&mdash;is now available to all Open Plan users.\n"
msgstr "Ang Heron r2 [`ibm_kingston`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_kingston)&mdash;isa sa aming pinaka-mataas ang performance na mga quantum computer&mdash;ay available na ngayon sa lahat ng Open Plan users.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Log 20 minutes of compute in any 12-month period and you can opt in to a special one-time offer: 180 minutes for the next 12 months.\n"
msgstr "Mag-log ng 20 minuto ng compute sa anumang 12-buwang panahon at maaari kang mag-opt in sa isang espesyal na one-time offer: 180 minuto para sa susunod na 12 buwan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "      With expanded runtime and new educational resources, users can run everything from introductory circuits to advanced hybrid workflows.\n"
msgstr "      Sa pinalawak na runtime at bagong mga educational resource, maaaring magpatakbo ang mga user ng lahat mula sa panimulang mga circuit hanggang sa advanced na hybrid workflows.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "      These efforts reflect our commitment to open access, open education, and open science in quantum computing. Read more: [Doubling down on open-access quantum computing](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/open-plan-updates)\n"
msgstr "      Sinasalamin ng mga pagsisikap na ito ang aming pangako sa open access, open education, at open science sa quantum computing. Magbasa pa: [Doubling down on open-access quantum computing](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/open-plan-updates)\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### Upcoming discontinuation of Qiskit Code Assistant service\n"
msgstr "  ### Upcoming discontinuation of Qiskit Code Assistant service\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  On 29 May 2026, IBM Quantum will discontinue the preview Qiskit Code Assistant service and archive the supporting extensions for Visual Studio Code and JupyterLab.\n"
msgstr "  Sa Mayo 29, 2026, ihihinto ng IBM Quantum ang preview na serbisyo ng Qiskit Code Assistant at aarkibuhin ang mga sumusuportang extension para sa Visual Studio Code at JupyterLab.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Based on feedback and usage patterns, more users are running Qiskit Code Assistant models locally and working in editor integrations that are already part of their development workflow.\n"
msgstr "  Batay sa feedback at pattern ng paggamit, mas maraming user ang nagpapatakbo ng mga modelo ng Qiskit Code Assistant nang lokal at gumagawa sa mga editor integration na bahagi na ng kanilang development workflow.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Qiskit Code Assistant models will remain available for local use. To continue using them, move to a local deployment and a community-supported editor integration or other local tooling.\n"
msgstr "  Mananatiling available ang mga modelo ng Qiskit Code Assistant para sa lokal na paggamit. Upang magpatuloy sa paggamit ng mga ito, lumipat sa isang lokal na deployment at isang editor integration na suportado ng komunidad o iba pang lokal na tooling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For setup guidance, see the [Qiskit Code Assistant](/guides/qiskit-code-assistant) guide.\n"
msgstr "  Para sa gabay sa setup, tingnan ang [Qiskit Code Assistant](/guides/qiskit-code-assistant) guide.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### Nighthawk arrives in the EU\n"
msgstr "  ### Nighthawk arrives in the EU\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Premium and Flex Plans now have early access to [`ibm_berlin`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_berlin)! It is the first IBM Quantum Nighthawk r1 QPU in the EU (`eu-de` region) and the second Nighthawk in our global fleet, after [`ibm_miami`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_miami) in the US (`us-east` region). `ibm_berlin` features faster two-qubit gates than `ibm_miami` (68 ns versus 138 ns, median) while maintaining similar fleet-leading coherence (T$_1$ of ~350 &#181;s).\n"
msgstr "  Ngayon ay may maagang access na ang Premium at Flex Plans sa [`ibm_berlin`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_berlin)! Ito ang unang IBM Quantum Nighthawk r1 QPU sa EU (`eu-de` region) at ang pangalawang Nighthawk sa aming global fleet, pagkatapos ng [`ibm_miami`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_miami) sa US (`us-east` region). Ang `ibm_berlin` ay may mas mabilis na two-qubit gates kaysa sa `ibm_miami` (68 ns kumpara sa 138 ns, median) habang pinapanatili ang katulad na fleet-leading coherence (T$_1$ na ~350 &#181;s).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Since its release, Nighthawk has enabled research in regimes where classical simulation becomes increasingly challenging. Specifically, its architecture supports hardware-efficient workflows that map naturally onto grid-based (lattice) models. See recent papers from [Phasecraft](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12236) and [Volkswagen](https://doi.org/10.3390/e28040367), and their collaborators, demonstrating simulation at scale on Nighthawk.\n"
msgstr "  Simula noong ilabas ito, pinagana ng Nighthawk ang pananaliksik sa mga rehimen kung saan ang klasikal na simulation ay lalong nagiging mahirap. Sa partikular, ang arkitektura nito ay sumusuporta sa hardware-efficient na mga workflow na natural na naaangkop sa mga grid-based (lattice) na modelo. Tingnan ang mga kamakailang papel mula sa [Phasecraft](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12236) at [Volkswagen](https://doi.org/10.3390/e28040367), at kanilang mga kolaborador, na nagpapakita ng simulation sa malaking sukat sa Nighthawk.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Please note that `ibm_berlin` is currently an exploratory QPU that is still being tested and optimized as part of our continual cycles of learning. As such, it temporarily has the following limitations:\n"
msgstr "  Pakitandaan na ang `ibm_berlin` ay kasalukuyang isang exploratory QPU na sinusubukan pa at ino-optimize bilang bahagi ng aming patuloy na siklo ng pag-aaral. Dahil dito, pansamantala itong may mga sumusunod na limitasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default repetition time has been temporarily increased from 250 &#181;s to 4 ms, which impacts QPU time required to execute workloads. Users can manually select a shorter repetition time, but performance might be degraded.\n"
msgstr "Pansamantalang tumaas ang default na repetition time mula 250 &#181;s tungong 4 ms, na nakakaapekto sa oras ng QPU na kailangan upang isagawa ang mga workload. Maaaring manwal na pumili ang mga user ng mas maikling repetition time, ngunit maaaring bumaba ang performance.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic circuits are not yet supported, and quality of mid-circuit measurements is limited.\n"
msgstr "Hindi pa suportado ang dynamic circuits, at limitado ang kalidad ng mid-circuit measurements.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### Upcoming retirements\n"
msgstr "  ### Upcoming retirements\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  As we expand EU capacity and roll out the latest Nighthawk and Heron processors, `ibm_brussels` and `ibm_strasbourg` are scheduled to be retired on or around 30 April 2026.\n"
msgstr "  Habang pinalalawak namin ang kapasidad sa EU at inilulunsad ang pinakabagong Nighthawk at Heron processors, naka-iskedyul na mag-retire ang `ibm_brussels` at `ibm_strasbourg` sa o malapit sa Abril 30, 2026.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Once these QPUs are retired, they will no longer accept jobs. If your workflows target `ibm_brussels` or `ibm_strasbourg`, please migrate to another active QPU ahead of the retirement date to take advantage of the latest systems. For guidance on retrieving data from past jobs, refer to the following [documentation](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"
msgstr "  Kapag na-retire na ang mga QPU na ito, hindi na sila tatanggap ng mga job. Kung nagta-target ang iyong mga workflow sa `ibm_brussels` o `ibm_strasbourg`, mangyaring lumipat sa ibang aktibong QPU bago ang petsa ng pagreretiro upang samantalahin ang pinakabagong mga sistema. Para sa gabay sa pagkuha ng datos mula sa mga nakaraang job, sumangguni sa sumusunod na [dokumentasyon](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### `ibm_torino` is now retired\n"
msgstr "  ### `ibm_torino` is now retired\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The quantum computer `ibm_torino` has been retired and will no longer accept workload submissions. Any workloads that were already queued on this QPU might still be processed and return results.\n"
msgstr "  Na-retire na ang quantum computer na `ibm_torino` at hindi na ito tatanggap ng mga pagsusumite ng workload. Ang anumang workload na naka-queue na sa QPU na ito ay maaari pa ring maproseso at magbigay ng mga resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If you would like to retrieve job data from important workloads run on this QPU, refer to [these instructions](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"
msgstr "  Kung gusto mong kunin ang job data mula sa mahahalagang workload na pinatakbo sa QPU na ito, sumangguni sa [mga tagubiling ito](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### ibm_brussels and ibm_strasbourg are now retired\n"
msgstr "  ### ibm_brussels and ibm_strasbourg are now retired\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  `ibm_brussels` and `ibm_strasbourg` have been retired and will no longer accept jobs.\n"
msgstr "  Na-retire na ang `ibm_brussels` at `ibm_strasbourg` at hindi na sila tatanggap ng mga job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This change is part of the continued evolution and expansion of the IBM Quantum fleet in the EU, including the recently released Nighthawk QPU [`ibm_berlin`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_berlin) and the upgraded Heron r3 QPU [`ibm_aachen`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_aachen). The global fleet has now fully transitioned away from Eagle, IBM Quantum's first utility‑scale processor family, introduced in 2021.\n"
msgstr "  Bahagi ang pagbabagong ito ng patuloy na ebolusyon at pagpapalawak ng IBM Quantum fleet sa EU, kabilang ang kamakailang inilabas na Nighthawk QPU na [`ibm_berlin`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_berlin) at ang na-upgrade na Heron r3 QPU na [`ibm_aachen`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_aachen). Ganap nang lumipat ang global fleet mula sa Eagle, ang unang pamilya ng utility-scale processor ng IBM Quantum, na inilabas noong 2021.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If your workflows target `ibm_brussels` or `ibm_strasbourg`, please migrate to another active QPU to take advantage of the latest hardware. For guidance on retrieving data from past jobs, refer to the [documentation](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"
msgstr "  Kung nagta-target ang iyong mga workflow sa `ibm_brussels` o `ibm_strasbourg`, mangyaring lumipat sa ibang aktibong QPU upang samantalahin ang pinakabagong hardware. Para sa gabay sa pagkuha ng datos mula sa mga nakaraang job, sumangguni sa [dokumentasyon](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "March 2026 {#march-2026}"
msgstr "March 2026 {#march-2026}"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The EU gets its first Heron r3 {#the-eu-gets-its-first-heron-r3}"
msgstr "The EU gets its first Heron r3 {#the-eu-gets-its-first-heron-r3}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Maintenance has been completed on [`ibm_aachen`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_aachen) and the QPU is now back online in the eu‑de region.  `ibm_aachen` has also been upgraded to be the first QPU in the EU to feature the latest [Heron r3](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/jay-gambetta-a274753a_following-up-on-an-earlier-post-https-activity-7364268815720824834-aZ0k) processor. It is the third r3 in our global fleet, after [`ibm_boston`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_boston) and [`ibm_pittsburgh`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_pittsburgh) in the US.\n"
msgstr "  Nakumpleto na ang maintenance sa [`ibm_aachen`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_aachen) at nasa online na muli ang QPU sa eu-de region. Na-upgrade na rin ang `ibm_aachen` upang maging unang QPU sa EU na may pinakabagong [Heron r3](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/jay-gambetta-a274753a_following-up-on-an-earlier-post-https-activity-7364268815720824834-aZ0k) processor. Ito ang ikatlong r3 sa aming global fleet, pagkatapos ng [`ibm_boston`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_boston) at [`ibm_pittsburgh`](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers?system=ibm_pittsburgh) sa US.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Heron r3 continues to deliver improved error rates and overall system performance compared to Heron r2, demonstrating more reliable execution and better results for workloads. For example, on `ibm_aachen`, we observe a large boost in $T_2$ (phase coherence time) from 150&nbsp;&#181;s to 250&nbsp;&#181;s. You can view metrics like these for all QPUs in the shared fleet on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page.\n"
msgstr "  Patuloy na naghahatid ang Heron r3 ng pinahusay na error rates at kabuuang performance ng sistema kumpara sa Heron r2, na nagpapakita ng mas maaasahang pagpapatupad at mas magandang resulta para sa mga workload. Halimbawa, sa `ibm_aachen`, napapansin namin ang malaking pagtaas sa $T_2$ (phase coherence time) mula 150&nbsp;&#181;s tungong 250&nbsp;&#181;s. Maaari mong tingnan ang mga sukatang tulad nito para sa lahat ng QPU sa shared fleet sa [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "February 2026 {#february-2026}"
msgstr "February 2026 {#february-2026}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### `ibm_torino` to retire\n"
msgstr "  ### `ibm_torino` to retire\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The `ibm_torino` QPU will retire on or around 1 April 2026. Once this QPU is retired, it will no longer accept jobs.\n"
msgstr "  Magre-retire ang `ibm_torino` QPU sa o malapit sa Abril 1, 2026. Kapag na-retire na ang QPU na ito, hindi na ito tatanggap ng mga job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  If you would like to retrieve job data from important past jobs, please refer to the following [documentation](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"
msgstr "  Kung gusto mong kunin ang job data mula sa mahahalagang nakaraang job, mangyaring sumangguni sa sumusunod na [dokumentasyon](/guides/retired-qpus#retrieve-a-job-from-a-retired-qpu).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  ### Increase in repetition delay time maximum\n"
msgstr "  ### Increase in repetition delay time maximum\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  To provide more flexibility for users, we have expanded the allowable repetition delay time range from 20-500 &#181;s to 20-2000 &#181;s on our Heron and Eagle QPUs. The Nighthawk QPU delay time range continues to be 1000-4000 &#181;s as previously announced. Note that if you choose to increase repetition delay (`rep_delay`), it will have a direct impact on your execution time and capacity consumption, but it might improve the fidelity of certain circuits. The default `rep_delay` remains unchanged on all QPUs.\n"
msgstr "  Upang magbigay ng mas maraming kakayahang umangkop para sa mga user, pinalawak namin ang pinapayagang saklaw ng repetition delay time mula 20-500 &#181;s tungong 20-2000 &#181;s sa aming mga Heron at Eagle QPU. Ang saklaw ng delay time ng Nighthawk QPU ay nananatiling 1000-4000 &#181;s tulad ng dati nang inanunsyo. Tandaan na kung pipiliin mong dagdagan ang repetition delay (`rep_delay`), magkakaroon ito ng direktang epekto sa iyong oras ng pagpapatupad at pagkonsumo ng kapasidad, ngunit maaari nitong mapabuti ang fidelity ng ilang mga circuit. Nananatiling hindi nagbabago ang default na `rep_delay` sa lahat ng QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  You can find more information about repetition delay time, including how to change it, in [Qubit initialization](/guides/repetition-rate-execution).\n"
msgstr "  Makakahanap ka ng karagdagang impormasyon tungkol sa repetition delay time, kabilang kung paano ito baguhin, sa [Qubit initialization](/guides/repetition-rate-execution).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "January 2026 {#january-2026}"
msgstr "January 2026 {#january-2026}"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The latest enhancements to the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page include the following:\n"
msgstr "Kasama sa pinakabagong mga pagpapahusay sa [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Unified QPU view** - All QPUs across regions are now displayed in a single table, making it easier to see status and calibrations of the shared fleet across the two regions. (You can still filter the Compute resources table by region using the funnel icon.)\n"
msgstr "**Unified QPU view** - Ipinapakita na ngayon ang lahat ng QPU sa lahat ng rehiyon sa isang solong table, na ginagawang mas madaling makita ang status at calibrations ng shared fleet sa dalawang rehiyon. (Maaari mo pa ring i-filter ang Compute resources table ayon sa rehiyon gamit ang funnel icon.)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Single maintenance schedule** - The maintenance schedule is now at the top of the page, even when no events are currently planned.\n"
msgstr "**Single maintenance schedule** - Nasa itaas na ngayon ng page ang maintenance schedule, kahit walang kasalukuyang naka-iskedyul na mga event.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**\"Instance access\" details** - When viewing a QPU's details, a new Instance access section shows all instances that grant the user access to that QPU for the selected account.\n"
msgstr "**\"Instance access\" details** - Kapag tinitingnan ang mga detalye ng isang QPU, isang bagong Instance access section ang nagpapakita ng lahat ng instances na nagbibigay ng access sa user para sa QPU na iyon para sa napiling account.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The first Nighthawk QPU and latest Heron QPU are now available.** These two powerful new processors debuted at the [IBM Quantum Developer Conference](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qdc-2025) in November.\n"
msgstr "**The first Nighthawk QPU and latest Heron QPU are now available.** Ang dalawang makapangyarihang bagong processor na ito ay unang inilabas sa [IBM Quantum Developer Conference](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/blog/qdc-2025) noong Nobyembre.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Premium and Flex Plans now have early access to `ibm_miami`, the first IBM Quantum Nighthawk QPU. Our most advanced quantum processor to date, Nighthawk is a 120-qubit device with a square-lattice topology (218 couplers versus Heron's 176) that is designed to support more complex workloads. Nighthawk has the highest coherence of our fleet - even higher than what was reported at QDC - with a median T1 of 350 &#181;s.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon ay may maagang access na ang Premium at Flex Plans sa `ibm_miami`, ang unang IBM Quantum Nighthawk QPU. Ang aming pinaka-advanced na quantum processor sa ngayon, ang Nighthawk ay isang 120-qubit na device na may square-lattice topology (218 couplers kumpara sa 176 ng Heron) na dinisenyo upang suportahan ang mas kumplikadong mga workload. May pinakamataas na coherence ang Nighthawk sa aming fleet - mas mataas pa nga kaysa sa iniulat sa QDC - na may median T1 na 350 &#181;s.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that `ibm_miami` is currently an exploratory QPU that is still being tested and optimized as part of our continual cycles of learning. As such, it temporarily has the following limitations:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang `ibm_miami` ay kasalukuyang isang exploratory QPU na sinusubukan pa at ino-optimize bilang bahagi ng aming patuloy na siklo ng pag-aaral. Dahil dito, pansamantala itong may mga sumusunod na limitasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Default repetition time has been temporarily increased from 250 &#181;s to 4 ms, which will impact QPU time required to execute workloads\n"
msgstr "Pansamantalang tumaas ang default na repetition time mula 250 &#181;s tungong 4 ms, na makakaapekto sa oras ng QPU na kailangan upang isagawa ang mga workload\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamic circuits are not yet supported, and quality of mid-circuit measurements is limited\n"
msgstr "Hindi pa suportado ang dynamic circuits, at limitado ang kalidad ng mid-circuit measurements\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additionally, Premium, Flex, and Pay-As-You-Go Plans now have access to `ibm_boston`, our most performant IBM Quantum Heron r3 to date. It has demonstrated an EPLG at 100 qubits of 2.15e-3, with 57 of 176 possible two-qubit gates below the 1e-3 error level.\n"
msgstr "Bukod dito, may access na ngayon ang Premium, Flex, at Pay-As-You-Go Plans sa `ibm_boston`, ang aming pinaka-mahusay na IBM Quantum Heron r3 sa ngayon. Nagpakita ito ng EPLG sa 100 qubits na 2.15e-3, na may 57 sa 176 posibleng two-qubit gates na mas mababa sa 1e-3 error level.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Introducing instance archiving for administrators on IBM Quantum Platform.** With this update, administrators can archive any instance within their account. Archiving an instance ensures that:\n"
msgstr "**Introducing instance archiving for administrators on IBM Quantum Platform.** Sa update na ito, maaaring i-archive ng mga administrator ang anumang instance sa loob ng kanilang account. Tinitiyak ng pag-archive ng isang instance na:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collaborators retain access to results and QPU metrics, properties, and calibrations from past workloads.\n"
msgstr "Mananatiling may access ang mga kolaborador sa mga resulta at QPU metrics, properties, at calibrations mula sa mga nakaraang workload.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "No new workloads can be submitted to the archived instance, preventing unintended usage.\n"
msgstr "Walang bagong workload na maaaring isumite sa naka-archive na instance, na pumipigil sa hindi sinasadyang paggamit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Archived instances do not subtract anything from your account's plan allocation.\n"
msgstr "Hindi nagbabawas ang mga naka-archive na instance ng anuman mula sa allocation ng plano ng iyong account.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "All archived instances are neatly organized under a dedicated \"Archived\" tab.\n"
msgstr "Maayos na naka-organisa ang lahat ng naka-archive na instance sa ilalim ng dedikadong tab na \"Archived\".\n"

#. type: Bullet: '      - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administrators can reactivate an instance at any time.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring i-reactivate ng mga administrator ang isang instance anumang oras.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "[**Directed execution model.**](/guides/directed-execution-model) This new execution model allows you to fine-tune error mitigation and other techniques without sacrificing performance by providing the ingredients to capture design intents on the client side, and shifting the costly generation of circuit variants to the server side. For example, you can use the [Samplomatic library](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html) to define the exact layers in your circuits to apply Pauli-twirling and to inject noise. The new [Executor primitive](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive) will then follow your directives to generate and execute the randomized circuit variants in Qiskit Runtime.\n"
msgstr "[**Directed execution model.**](/guides/directed-execution-model) Pinapayagan ng bagong execution model na ito na i-fine-tune ang error mitigation at iba pang mga teknik nang hindi isinasakripisyo ang performance sa pamamagitan ng pagbibigay ng mga sangkap upang mahuli ang mga design intent sa panig ng client, at ilipat ang mamahaling generation ng mga circuit variant sa panig ng server. Halimbawa, maaari mong gamitin ang [Samplomatic library](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/index.html) upang tukuyin ang eksaktong mga layer sa iyong mga circuit para maglapat ng Pauli-twirling at mag-inject ng noise. Susundan ng bagong [Executor primitive](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive) ang iyong mga direktiba upang makabuo at magpatupad ng mga randomized circuit variant sa Qiskit Runtime.\n"

